In the one-spin Hilbert space, the proposition that $\sigma_3=+1$ corresponds to the one-dimensional subspace spanned by $\ket{u}$. Its projector acts as $P_{\sigma_3=+1}
  \begin{pmatrix}\alpha\\\beta\end{pmatrix}
  =
  \begin{pmatrix}\alpha\\0\end{pmatrix},
  \qquad
  P_{\sigma_3=-1}
  \begin{pmatrix}\alpha\\\beta\end{pmatrix}
  =
  \begin{pmatrix}0\\\beta\end{pmatrix}.$

