For $A\wedge\neg B$, electron 1 must be up along the third axis and electron 2 must be up along $\hat n_{45}=\frac{\hat x+\hat z}{\sqrt2}.$ The relevant component of the second spin is $\boldsymbol{\tau}\cdot\hat n_{45}
  =
  \frac{\tau_1+\tau_3}{\sqrt2}.$ The joint projector is therefore $P_{A\wedge\neg B}
  =
  \frac{I+\sigma_3}{2}
  \frac{I+(\tau_1+\tau_3)/\sqrt2}{2}.$

